cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use must, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "must: Multiple-Stressor Interactions Under Alternative Null Models"
version: 0.2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Amador Crespo
    given-names: Pablo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3793-8794"
abstract: >-
  Detects and classifies non-additive effects of multiple stressors in
  experiments, testing each combination of stressors against alternative
  null models with the same criteria. Before any model is fitted, the design
  is described: missing treatment combinations, cells shared by several
  contrasts, replication units and repeated measures, and which
  interactions it identifies. Interactions are tested from the adjusted
  predictions of one model per response, by default with a small-sample
  correction. The null models are simple addition (the default), the
  multiplicative and dominance models, Bliss independence, the stress
  addition model and concentration addition. For three or more stressors
  the net deviation from the single-stressor effects is distinguished from
  the pure highest-order interaction, and interactions can be classified
  with the directional scheme of Piggott et al. (2015).
keywords:
  - multiple stressors
  - stressor interactions
  - null models
  - synergism
  - antagonism
  - ecology
  - ecotoxicology
  - R
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pabloamadorc/must"
url: "https://pabloamadorc.github.io/must/"
